A few questions come to mind.  First, is the area of defamation law and 
publication crossing international boundaries covered by treaty or local 
laws and in which jurisdiction?  If a carrier cannot be sued in Canada, but 
can be sued in England (residence of plaintiff and where the alleged 
defamation was published), which rules will govern and does it depend upon 
