Indeed, the binary groups are not all violations, but some binary groups
are mostly violations, and groups that are mostly violations must be taken
from your system if you want to avoid participation in organized
copyright violation.

(And it doesn't matter whether it says violations in the newsgroups file
or not.  What matters is the content of the group.   If you read these
newsgroups you can't claim you were ignorant of the violations any more.)

That also applies to a lot of FTP libraries, and it certainly applies to
some, but not all, of the non-sexual picture groups and sound sample groups.

The thing that distinguishes these groups is actually pretty clear.  Almost
all newsgroups exist for people to post stuff they wrote.

These groups exist primarily to post stuff the poster didn't create.  We
