------------------------------------------------------------------

               The Internet Can Positively Shine !
               -----------------------------------
                    by Michael S. Eggley
                         12/16/93
         
One of the more common occurrences in the Internet vocabulary
happens to be the word "flame", and all of it's possible forms:

 "I posted something stupid and got flamed...OUCH!"
 "A flame-war broke out regarding our new pricing policy..."
 "This board is known for its flaming..."
 "Be careful or you'll get flamed..."
 "...Hmm...I'll just flame him into submission..."

Anyone with experience on the net realizes the negative connotation
this word carries.  Its usage is legitimate in many cases, but I
feel its negativity unfortunately spills over into other aspects of
the Internet. 

That is why I propose the introduction of a new term into the
Internet vocabulary:  "shine".  This term would become the
direct antecedent of "flame", and carry with it a positive
connotation in every context.  Examples:

  "He shined me, I sent my thoughts to my boss, and he shined me !"
  "Fearing a flame, instead I was shined by all who responded..."
  "That idea is shinin' !..."
  "Wow ! That is one ultra-shinin' idea !"
  "Hoping for a shine, I ended up getting flamed !"
  "That last post was a real shiner...thanks for the info!"
  "The new gopher at xxx.xxx.edu casts a bright shine on the      
     net..."
  "We quelled the flames with logic and reason and ended up       
     shining.......Ahhhhhhh"
  
One might feel that the above dissertation is a result of too many
sleepless nights on the net, and leaving with a negative feeling.
That is partially true.  So, let's accentuate the positive.  Let's
do everything possible to put a high-gloss "shine" to the nearly
limitless positive aspects out there in cyberspace.....


Michael S. Eggley
Director of Information Systems and Goofy Word Association
Iowa Network Services, Inc.
