As there appears to be some confusion about Godfrey and free speech
on the net, I want to outline the situation as I see it.

The right of all users of the net to freely express their views
is absolute.  Godfrey included, of course.  However, this is not 
the point at issue.  The crux of the matter is whether you want 
to continue to enjoy access to the net through your University's 
or Employer's computers.

If Godfrey wins a libel case, brought due to statements made on the net,
this will set a legal precedent.  Many Universities and Employers around 
the world are going to conclude that the financial risk (i.e. libel 
awards and legal costs) of giving net access to their students or 
employees makes continued net access just not worthwhile.
They will therefore, logically, remove net access from their sites.

If you don't mind losing your access to the groups you post to,
then that is fine, don't complain about Godfrey, 
but if you care about the future of a free international net, 
with many different subscribers, then perhaps you should do something now.

Jason

